# [Skeleton generator]($heading.id('skeleton-generator'))

```sh
php tools/phpz_skel.php --help
php tools/phpz_skel.php --ext my_php_extension --phpz 0.1.0
```

Run the second command from the phpz repository root. It creates `my_php_extension` in the current directory and pins the phpz dependency to the `0.1.0` tag.

| Option | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `--ext` | Extension name; required |
| `--dir` | Parent directory for the generated project |
| `--phpz` | Package URL passed to `zig fetch --save=phpz`; a bare name is treated as a phpz tag |
| `--zig` | Path to the Zig executable |
| `--with-php-config` | Path to `php-config` for locating PHP development headers |
| `--with-php-build-system` | Generate PHP build system integration files |
| `--onlyunix` / `--onlywindows` | Generate support only for the selected platform |
| `--force` | Overwrite generated template files in the target directory |

# [Build]($heading.id('build'))

Run these commands from the generated extension directory:

```sh
zig build -Dphp-include-dir="$(php-config --include-dir)"
zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSafe -Dphp-include-dir="$(php-config --include-dir)"
```

The default Debug mode helps locate errors during development. `ReleaseSafe` keeps Zig runtime safety checks enabled. The PHP runtime that loads the extension must match the headers used to compile it.

# [Generate arginfo]($heading.id('generate-arginfo'))

```sh
zig build gen-stub
```

This step copies the php-src `gen_stub.php` supplied by the phpz package to `build/gen_stub.php`, then processes the extension's Stub. The first run may need to download PHP-Parser, so it needs a writable `build/` directory and the corresponding download tools. Do not keep custom changes in the tool copy that this step updates.

Besides the bundled copy, you can run the script from a matching php-src checkout directly:

```sh
php /path/to/php-src/build/gen_stub.php my_php_extension.stub.php
```

# [PHPT tests]($heading.id('phpt-tests'))

```sh
zig build run-tests -Dphp-include-dir="$(php-config --include-dir)"
```

This step builds the extension, then updates the project's `run-tests.php` from the phpz package's `tools/php/run-tests.php` (from php-src), and runs the tests. To select a test, build the extension and invoke the project copy directly:

```sh
php run-tests.php -q --show-diff -d extension=modules/my_php_extension.so tests/greet.phpt
```

You can also run the script from a matching php-src checkout directly:

```sh
php /path/to/php-src/run-tests.php -q --show-diff -d extension=modules/my_php_extension.so tests/greet.phpt
```

Common PHPT sections include `--TEST--`, `--FILE--`, and `--EXPECT--`. For failures, read the actual output and diff. Record skips caused by a missing CGI binary separately from passing behavior tests.

